== (C3) parity-word bijection mod 2^k: constant shifts vs the strategy -chi_{-4} ==
   T_+1: bijection for k <= 12: True
   T_-1: bijection for k <= 12: True
      k=2: 3 distinct words among 4 residues
      k=3: 4 distinct words among 8 residues
      k=4: 5 distinct words among 16 residues
      k=5: 6 distinct words among 32 residues
      k=6: 7 distinct words among 64 residues
      k=7: 8 distinct words among 128 residues
      k=8: 9 distinct words among 256 residues
      k=9: 10 distinct words among 512 residues
      k=10: 11 distinct words among 1024 residues
   -chi_{-4} strategy (sigma(1 mod 4) = -1, sigma(3 mod 4) = +1): bijection for k <= 10: False
